findings.reasoning:
This is a false positive. Line 315 creates a multiprocessing.Queue object with a size parameter (1000). While multiprocessing.Queue does use pickle for serialization by default, this is not a deserialization vulnerability (CWE-502) because: (1) The queue is used for inter-process communication within the same trusted application, (2) The data being serialized consists of internal library objects (GetObjectJob, SHUTDOWN_SIGNAL) created by the library itself, not untrusted external data, (3) CWE-502 specifically requires deserialization of untrusted data, which is not present here. The CodeQL query appears to be flagging all multiprocessing.Queue usage as a precautionary measure, but this specific instance does not represent an actual vulnerability.</reasoning>
